## Applications

Two-way ANOVA is commonly used in education, agriculture, psychology, healthcare research, and business analytics.

It helps researchers understand the individual effects of two factors and whether those factors interact.

## Conclusion

Two-way ANOVA is useful for comparing outcomes across combinations of two categorical factors. Understanding the method and its assumptions is essential for drawing reliable conclusions.
